    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "2 Scilly Hill is a beautifully renovated semi-detached home set in the heart of the picturesque Scilly village. Positioned on the sought-after Ardbrack side of Scilly, the property enjoys the perfect balance of tranquillity and convenience. Located just a short stroll from the vibrant centre of Kinsale town yet tucked away in a peaceful setting with an almost countryside feel. The panoramic views over Kinsale Harbour, the town and the historic forts are truly exceptional."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Originally a traditional fisherman’s cottage, the property now extends to c. 142 sqm of beautifully designed living accommodation laid out over three floors. In recent years, the house has been extensively renovated and modernised to an exceptional standard, creating a stylish and comfortable home while retaining its original charm and character.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor features a stunning bespoke contemporary kitchen and a separate dining area ideal for entertaining. A thoughtfully designed extension to the original house incorporates a fully fitted utility room and a beautifully finished, fully tiled shower room. Also on this level is a warm and inviting sitting room centered around a solid fuel stove. The first floor accommodates three spacious double bedrooms and a stylish family bathroom. One bedroom is presently in use as a dressing room with extensive built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nOn the top floor, there is a large bedroom en-suite together with a separate study, offering an ideal private master suite with work-from-home space.\r\n\r\nThroughout the property, exceptional attention to detail is evident, with high-quality finishes including custom-built furniture, premium sanitary ware, fully tiled bathrooms and quality carpeting. Every room enjoys breathtaking views over the harbour and surrounding landscape.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from a private enclosed garden, paved terrace area and outdoor storage shed, perfectly designed for al fresco dining while taking in the spectacular harbour views."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Sea View"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: D2"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Location",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "2 Scilly Hill is located in Scilly, which still offers the quaint, relaxed atmosphere of the fishing village it once was, and today is one of the most sought after locations in Kinsale. Located a few minutes walk from the pretty seaside town of Kinsale and a mere 25 minutes drive from the cosmopolitan city of Cork Scilly Hill offers lovely views across the harbour and Castlepark peninsula from its elevated position.\r\n\r\nThis area of South West Ireland is of outstanding beauty with its dramatic coastline, unspoilt locations and safe beaches. Leisure activities are well catered for, Kinsale provides excellent sailing, yachting and fishing facilities from its two marinas. There are three world class golf courses including the renowned Old Head of Kinsale. Other recreational pursuits include walking, bathing, surfing, and horse riding. There are numerous cultural events held throughout the year, such as the world famous Kinsale Arts Festival, the Cork Jazz Festival, Cork Film Festival, Kinsale Gourmet Festival along with a thriving music and opera programme. Cork has several fine theatres, and Cork Opera House hosts many exceptional productions throughout the year. Kinsale is also home to some of Ireland’s finest restaurants, contributing to its title as Gourmet Capital of Ireland; along with many top class hotels and lots of welcoming pubs.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is conveniently located 20 minutes drive from Kinsale with direct links within Ireland and to major European and UK cities."
      },
      {
